Running -eval TCL: help config_interface
SYNTAX 
  config_interface [OPTIONS]

DESCRIPTION
  The config_interface command specifies the default interface options used to implement the RTL ports of each function.

OPTIONS
  -clock_enable [=true|*false*]
    Add a clock-enable port (ap_ce) to the design. The clock enable prevents all clock operations when it is active low:
    disables all sequential operations
  -default_slave_interface <none|*s_axilite*>
    Default slave interface
  -m_axi_addr64 [=false|*true*]
    Enable 64-bit addressing for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_alignment_byte_size <uint:*1*> 
    Specify size to align to for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_auto_id_channel [=true|*false*]
    Enable automatic assignment of channel IDs for m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_auto_max_ports [=true|*false*]
    Enable automatic creation of m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_buffer_impl <auto|lutram|uram|*bram*>
    Select implmentation for all m_axi internal buffers
      auto : Automatic selection
      lutram : Distributed RAM
      bram : Block RAM (default)
      uram : Ultra RAM
  -m_axi_cache_impl <lutram|bram|uram|*auto*>
    Select implmentation for m_axi internal caches
      auto : Automatic selection (default)
      lutram : Distributed RAM
      bram : Block RAM
      uram : Ultra RAM
  -m_axi_conservative_mode [=false|*true*]
    Configure all m_axi adaptors to work in conservative mode, waiting for all data to be written before a burst is started
  -m_axi_flush_mode [=true|*false*]
    Configure all m_axi adaptors to be flushable, writing or reading garbage data if a burst is interrupted due to pipeline
    blocking (missing data inputs when not in conservative mode or missing output space)
  -m_axi_latency <uint:*0*> 
    Specify the default latency value for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_max_bitwidth <uint:*1024*> 
    Specify the maximum data size in bits for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_max_read_burst_length <uint:*16*> 
    Specify the default max_read_burst_length value for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_max_widen_bitwidth <uint:*0*> 
    Specify the maximum data widening size in bits for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_max_write_burst_length <uint:*16*> 
    Specify the default max_write_burst_length value for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_min_bitwidth <uint:*8*> 
    Specify the minimum data size in bits for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_num_read_outstanding <uint:*16*> 
    Specify the default num_read_outstanding value for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_num_write_outstanding <uint:*16*> 
    Specify the default num_write_outstanding value for all m_axi interfaces
  -m_axi_offset <off|direct|*slave*>
    Specify the default offset for all m_axi interfaces
      off : No offset port generated
      direct : Generate a scalar input offset port
      slave : Generate an offset port and automatically map it to AXILite slave (default)
  -m_axi_register_io <all|*off*>
    Enable registers for all inputs/outputs inside m_axi adapter
      off : None of the m_axi inputs or outputs are registered (default)
      all : All m_axi inputs and outputs are registered.
  -register_io <scalar_in|scalar_out|scalar_all|*off*>
    Enable registers for all scalar inputs/outputs on the top function (arrays are always registered)
      off : None of the input or outputs are registered (default)
      scalar_in : All inputs are registered.
      scalar_out : All outputs are registered.
      scalar_all : All input and outputs are registered.
  -s_axilite_auto_restart_counter <1|*0*>
    Enables the creation of a counter that can control the number of times to restart the design.
      0 : No restart counter (default)
      1 : Enable restart counter
  -s_axilite_data64 [=true|*false*]
    Enable 64 bit data width for s_axilite interface
  -s_axilite_interrupt_mode <cor|*tow*>
    Select s_axilite interrupt mode
      cor : clearing s_axilite interrupt register when read
      tow : toggling s_axilite interrupt register when write (default)
  -s_axilite_mailbox <both|in|out|*none*>
    Enables the creation of a mailboxes for non-stream non-stable s_axilite arguments
      both : Enable mailbox for input and output arguments
      in : Enable mailbox for only input arguments
      out : Enable mailbox for only output arguments
      none : No mailbox created (default)
  -s_axilite_status_regs <ecc|*off*>
    Enables exposure of ECC error bits in the SAXILite register file via two clear-on-read counters per BRAM or URAM with
    ECC enabled
      off : No status registers generated (default)
      ecc : Enable counters for ECC errors for BRAMs and URAMs
  -s_axilite_sw_reset [=true|*false*]
    Enable SW reset in s_axilite adapter

